# Line endings: LF in the repository and in every checkout, on every OS.
# Prettier, rustfmt and the generated-code drift check compare bytes, so a CRLF checkout (Git for
# Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true) would fail them. Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff2 binary
*.bundle binary
